; DEV/TEST-ONLY FIXTURE ZONE — NOT real DNS data. See ../Corefile (the mxservfail.test block) and
; deploy/dns-test/README.md. The name exists and publishes an SPF record with a bare `mx` mechanism, but
; its MX query is made to SERVFAIL by the Corefile's `template IN MX` — there is deliberately NO MX
; record here, because the answer to an MX query for this name is not "none", it is "failed".

$ORIGIN mxservfail.test.
$TTL 300

@       IN SOA  ns.mxservfail.test. admin.mxservfail.test. (
                2026110801 ; serial
                3600       ; refresh
                900        ; retry
                604800     ; expire
                60 )       ; negative-cache TTL
@       IN NS   ns.mxservfail.test.
ns      IN A    127.0.0.1

@       IN TXT  "v=spf1 mx -all"
